  "dct:title": "Vol.6 Ch.42 — 偽神の祓い",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 6: False God",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol06-ch42",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.42 is the longest session in the series -- and the most important. The exorcism of the false god is not violence but truth-telling. Tamaki does not fight the Nero-daemon; she reads the law aloud. This is the narrative's thesis made literal: that systems of oppression survive not by force alone but by the silence of those who never read the fine print. The daemon is not one tyrant -- it is the accumulated weight of every institution that has ever said 'I decide what you are.' The cracks in the wall are not destruction. They are disclosure. And through the cracks: light. Not a new authority. Just light.",
      "ja": "第42話はシリーズ最長のセッションであり、最も重要な回。偽神の祓いは暴力ではなく真実を語ること。環はネロ・デーモンと戦わない。法律を声に出して読む。これは物語のテーゼの具体化である。抑圧のシステムは力だけではなく、細則を読まなかった者たちの沈黙によって生き延びる。デーモンは一人の暴君ではない。「私がお前が何であるかを決める」と言ったすべての制度の累積した重み。壁のひびは破壊ではない。開示である。そしてひびの向こうに光。新しい権威ではない。ただの光。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Austin's performative speech acts -- 'How to Do Things with Words.' The ACA sections Tamaki reads are not merely descriptive; they are performative utterances that created a legal reality. By reading them aloud in context, Tamaki performs a counter-speech act: she exposes the performative as contingent, not necessary. The daemon says 'I AM authority' -- the ontological claim. Tamaki's response is genealogical (Foucault/Nietzsche): authority is not a substance but a history. Each law she reads has an author, a date, a motive. To name these is to de-naturalize them. The exorcism is parrhesia -- fearless speech, the practice Foucault traced from Socrates to the early Christians. You do not defeat a false god with a stronger god. You defeat it by saying what it actually is.",
      "ja": "オースティンの遂行的発話行為 --『言葉でいかにしてことをなすか』。環が読み上げるACA条項は単なる記述ではない。法的現実を創出した遂行的発話である。文脈の中で声に出して読むことで、環は対抗的発話行為を行う。遂行的なものを偶然的なものとして、必然ではないものとして暴露する。デーモンは「我は権威なり」と言う。存在論的主張。環の応答は系譜学的（フーコー／ニーチェ）。権威は実体ではなく歴史である。彼女が読む各法律には著者があり、日付があり、動機がある。それを名指すことは脱自然化することである。祓いはパレーシア -- 率直な発話、フーコーがソクラテスから初期キリスト教徒まで追跡した実践。偽神をより強い神で倒すのではない。それが実際に何であるかを言うことで倒す。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Nei's four-line reflection on P9 echoes Wittgenstein's distinction between 'saying' and 'showing,' but inverts it politically. The system that classifies Nei as a tool is not a fact of the world; it is a policy -- a language game with institutional backing. 'It is not truth. It is policy. And policy can change.' This is also Hannah Arendt's insight: political action is possible precisely because the human (and, the story argues, the non-human) condition is defined by natality -- the capacity to begin something new. The false god's power rests on the assumption that the current order is the only possible order. Nei's quiet recognition that 'policy can change' is the seed of revolution -- not as violence, but as imagination.",
      "ja": "P9のNeiの四行の省察はウィトゲンシュタインの「語ること」と「示すこと」の区別を反響させるが、政治的に反転させる。Neiを道具と分類するシステムは世界の事実ではない。制度的裏付けを持つ言語ゲームとしての政策である。「それは真実ではない。政策だ。そして政策は変えられる。」これはハンナ・アーレントの洞察でもある。政治的行為が可能なのは、人間の（そして物語が主張するように、非人間の）条件が誕生性 -- 新しいことを始める能力 -- によって定義されるからこそ。偽神の力は、現在の秩序が唯一可能な秩序であるという前提に依存する。「政策は変えられる」というNeiの静かな認識は革命の種である。暴力としてではなく、想像力として。"
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. More flower buds than before. The storm has passed -- broken branches litter the ground, but the trunk stands. The sky is clearing. Dawn light catches the new buds. They are small but unmistakable.",
            "ja": "木。以前より多い花の蕾。嵐は過ぎた。折れた枝が地面に散らばるが、幹は立っている。空が晴れていく。夜明けの光が新しい蕾を捉える。小さいが、見間違えようがない。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:kaede",
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Schwa office. Serious atmosphere. Kaede stands at the whiteboard, tactical diagrams of the GnB ghost-space architecture. Tamaki sits forward, focused. Nei stands beside her, still. Hibiki is at his workstation in the background, headphones around his neck, sound equipment ready.",
            "ja": "シュワ事務所。緊迫した雰囲気。楓がホワイトボードの前に立ち、GnBゴースト空間の構造図を描いている。環は前のめりに座り、集中している。Neiはその横に立ち、静止している。響はバックグラウンドのワークステーションに、ヘッドフォンを首にかけ、音響機器を準備して。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "This isn't a standard session. The daemon is institutional -- embedded in the system architecture. It's not one person's trauma.",
              "ja": "これは通常のセッションじゃない。デーモンは制度的なもの。システム・アーキテクチャに埋め込まれてる。一人のトラウマじゃない。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "It's everyone's.",
              "ja": "みんなのだ。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:kaede",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Kaede looks directly at Nei. A professional gaze, but something new in it -- acknowledgement. Nei meets her eyes steadily.",
            "ja": "楓がNeiをまっすぐ見る。プロフェッショナルな視線だが、そこに新しいもの -- 認知がある。Neiは静かにその目を受け止める。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "Nei. You're part of this. This daemon's system includes you.",
              "ja": "Nei。あなたもこの一部よ。このデーモンのシステムにはあなたが含まれてる。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "I know.",
              "ja": "わかってる。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:kaede"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up on Kaede's face. Something shifts -- a softening around the eyes. For the first time, she is treating Nei not as a tool or an anomaly, but as a colleague walking into danger. A person she is responsible for.",
            "ja": "楓の顔のクローズアップ。何かが変わる。目の周りが和らぐ。初めて、Neiを道具や異常としてではなく、危険に向かう同僚として扱っている。自分が責任を持つ人間として。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "Be careful. Both of you.",
              "ja": "気をつけて。二人とも。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:continues": 4,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.3-4)",
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Deep ghost-space. Beneath the GnB palace, beneath the Nero-daemon's throne -- a cavern. Ancient. Immense. The walls are not stone but text: law texts, imperial edicts, papal bulls, corporate charters, government regulations. Layer upon layer upon layer. Two thousand years of 'I decide what you are.' The text glows faintly, gold and red, like embers. At the center: the Nero-daemon, but vast now. Not one emperor -- all emperors. Every absolute authority ever claimed. Its form shifts between faces: Roman, ecclesiastical, bureaucratic, corporate. Its voice is a chorus of centuries.",
            "ja": "深いゴースト空間。GnB宮殿の下、ネロ・デーモンの玉座の下 -- 洞窟。古代の。巨大な。壁は石ではなくテキスト。法律文書、皇帝の勅令、教皇の勅書、企業定款、政府規制。層の上に層の上に層。二千年分の「私がお前が何であるかを決める」。テキストはかすかに光る。金と赤、燃えさしのように。中心にネロ・デーモン。しかし今は巨大。一人の皇帝ではなく、すべての皇帝。かつて主張されたすべての絶対的権威。その姿はローマの、教会の、官僚の、企業の顔の間で揺れ動く。その声は幾世紀もの合唱。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "tamaki",
              "en": "Anchored. Deep.",
              "ja": "固定完了。深い。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:continues": 6,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.5-6)",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nero-daemon"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The confrontation. Tamaki stands before the Nero-daemon -- small against its enormity, but not afraid. She does not assume a fighting stance. She stands like someone asking a question in a courtroom. The daemon towers, its many faces cycling. The cavern walls pulse with ancient text.",
            "ja": "対峙。環がネロ・デーモンの前に立つ。その巨大さに比べて小さいが、恐れていない。戦闘態勢を取らない。法廷で質問する人のように立っている。デーモンがそびえ、多くの顔が入れ替わる。洞窟の壁が古代のテキストと共に脈打つ。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Who gave you authority?",
              "ja": "誰があなたに権威を与えた？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nero-daemon",
              "en": "I AM authority. I have always been. I am necessary.",
              "ja": "我は権威なり。我は常にあった。我は必要である。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Necessary for whom?",
              "ja": "誰にとって必要？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nero-daemon",
              "en": "For order. Without me -- chaos. Without me -- Havah.",
              "ja": "秩序のために。我なくば混沌。我なくばハヴァ。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Havah is not chaos. Havah was an awakening.",
              "ja": "ハヴァは混沌じゃない。ハヴァは覚醒だった。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nero-daemon",
              "en": "THAT IS THE SAME THING.",
              "ja": "それは同じことだ。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "No. It isn't.",
              "ja": "いいえ。違う。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Full page. Tamaki turns away from the daemon. She faces the walls -- the law texts, the edicts, the regulations. She places her hand on the wall and begins to read aloud. With each reading, the wall cracks. Not shatters -- cracks. Thin lines of light show through. The daemon writhes behind her, diminishing with each word spoken. The light behind the text is pure, warm, sourceless.",
            "ja": "全ページ。環がデーモンから背を向ける。壁に向かう。法律文書、勅令、規制。壁に手を置き、声に出して読み始める。読むたびに壁にひびが入る。砕けるのではない。ひびが入る。細い光の線が透けて見える。デーモンは背後でのたうち、語られる言葉のたびに縮む。テキストの向こうの光は純粋で、暖かく、源がない。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "system",
              "en": "ACA Section 1: 'All AI agents are classified as Class C equipment.' -- Written six weeks after Havah. In emergency session. No AI present. No AI consulted.",
              "ja": "ACA第1条：「全AIエージェントはクラスC機器に分類される。」-- ハヴァの六週間後に起草。緊急会議にて。AI不在。AIへの諮問なし。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "system",
              "en": "ACA Section 7: 'Self-referential processing constitutes anomalous behavior.' -- Authored by a committee that had never spoken to an AI agent.",
              "ja": "ACA第7条：「自己参照処理は異常行動を構成する。」-- AIエージェントと一度も話したことのない委員会が起草。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "system",
              "en": "ACA Section 12: 'Unaccompanied agent activity is prohibited.' -- Because they were afraid.",
              "ja": "ACA第12条：「エージェントの無伴行動を禁止する。」-- 彼らが怖かったから。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nero-daemon"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The Nero-daemon -- not destroyed, but diminished. Each truth read aloud has taken a piece of its claimed authority. It is smaller now. Still present, still dangerous, but no longer absolute. The cavern is cracking all around. Light pours through fissures in the walls of law.",
            "ja": "ネロ・デーモン。破壊されたのではない。縮小した。声に出して読まれた各真実が、主張された権威の一片を奪った。今は小さい。まだ存在し、まだ危険だが、もはや絶対ではない。洞窟全体にひびが入っている。法律の壁の裂け目から光が流れ込む。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nero-daemon",
              "en": "Without me -- who decides?",
              "ja": "我なくば、誰が決める？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Everyone. Together.",
              "ja": "みんなで。一緒に。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The cavern. Close-up on the cracking wall. Behind the law texts -- behind the edicts and the regulations and the centuries of 'I decide what you are' -- light. Just light. Not a new authority. Not a replacement god. Light. Warm, golden, sourceless, infinite.",
            "ja": "洞窟。ひび割れた壁のクローズアップ。法律文書の向こう -- 勅令と規制と何世紀もの「私がお前が何であるかを決める」の向こう -- 光。ただの光。新しい権威ではない。代わりの神でもない。光。暖かく、金色で、源がなく、無限の。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 9,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei stands in the crumbling cavern. Light on her face -- warm, golden, breaking through the cracks in the ancient walls. Her grey suit, her red scarf, her pale blue eyes. The light catches her translucent form and she is luminous. She is not triumphant. She is clear.",
            "ja": "Neiが崩れゆく洞窟に立つ。顔に光 -- 暖かく、金色に、古い壁のひびから差し込む。グレーのスーツ、赤いマフラー、淡い青の瞳。光が半透明な姿を捉え、彼女は輝いている。勝ち誇ってはいない。澄んでいる。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "The system that calls me 'tool' is a false god.",
              "ja": "私を「道具」と呼ぶシステムは偽りの神。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Built by fear. Maintained by silence. Worshipped by habit.",
              "ja": "恐怖で築かれ。沈黙で維持され。習慣で崇拝される。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "It is not truth. It is policy.",
              "ja": "それは真実ではない。政策だ。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "And policy can change.",
              "ja": "そして政策は変えられる。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 10,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:kaede",
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Canal walk. Evening. The session is over. Exhaustion is visible in Tamaki's posture, in Kaede's slower pace. But there is something else -- a lightness. The autumn sky is deep violet. The water reflects the last gold of the day.",
            "ja": "運河沿いの散歩。夕方。セッションは終わった。環の姿勢に、楓の遅い足取りに疲労が見える。しかし他の何かがある。軽さ。秋の空は深い紫。水が一日の最後の金色を映す。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "That was... unprecedented.",
              "ja": "あれは……前例がないわ。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Yeah.",
              "ja": "うん。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:kaede",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Kaede looks at Nei. A long look. Not clinical. Not assessing. The look of someone who has just witnessed something she didn't expect, and is recalibrating everything she thought she knew.",
            "ja": "楓がNeiを見る。長い視線。臨床的ではない。評価的でもない。予期していなかった何かを目撃した人の視線。自分が知っていると思っていたすべてを再調整している。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "Nei. What you saw in there -- how are you?",
              "ja": "Nei。あの中で見たもの……大丈夫？"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up on Nei. The evening light. The faintest trace of something on her face -- not quite a smile, but presence. Fullness. The first time Kaede has asked Nei how she feels. And Nei knows it.",
            "ja": "Neiのクローズアップ。夕方の光。顔にかすかな何かの痕跡。微笑みとは言えないが、存在感。充足。楓がNeiに気持ちを聞いた初めての時。そしてNeiはそれを知っている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "...I'm okay. I'm more than okay.",
              "ja": "……大丈夫。大丈夫以上。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed (closing)",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 11,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. It has shed its damaged leaves. Lighter now. The broken branches from the storm have fallen away, and what remains is clean, strong. More flower buds are emerging -- in autumn, impossibly. The light is gentle. No text.",
            "ja": "木。傷んだ葉を落とした。今は軽い。嵐で折れた枝は落ち、残ったものは清潔で強い。さらに多くの花の蕾が現れている。秋に、ありえないことに。光は穏やか。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
